    bigIdea: 'Myles Munroe was born in 1954 in Nassau, in a Bahamas that was still a British colony, and he grew up poor, one of eleven children, singing to a queen he had never seen. He read the Bible with a colonial subject’s eyes and saw in it a King, a Kingdom and a colony: Yahweh extending the rule of Heaven to the earth through people made to have dominion. From Bahamas Faith Ministries International he carried that message to the nations, the Kingdom and not a religion, dominion over the earth and never over other men, and the buried potential of every person and of every formerly colonized people, until he, his wife Ruth and seven others died in a plane crash on 9 November 2014.',
