    bigIdea: 'In Rediscovering the Kingdom Munroe argues that religion is man’s search for a God he has lost, while the Kingdom is Yahweh’s answer: His government extended from Heaven to the earth. Humanity was created to rule the earth for Him; at the Fall it lost not Heaven but dominion; and Jesus came preaching one message, the Kingdom, to restore it. Those who receive Him are not adherents of a religion but citizens and ambassadors of a government.',
    inApp: 'Read the opening chapters of Rediscovering the Kingdom, especially his pages on religion (pp. 8, 22-23), dominion (pp. 12-17) and the ambassador (pp. 122, 161, 174). Then read Matthew 4:17, Matthew 6:33 and 2 Corinthians 5:20, and weigh what he said by the Word: is the gospel Jesus preached a religion to join, or a Kingdom to enter?',
