    bigIdea: 'In God’s Big Idea (later reissued as Reclaiming God’s Original Purpose for Your Life) Munroe argues that Yahweh’s original intent was to extend His Kingdom from Heaven to the earth, not by conquest but by planting a garden and filling it with people who would live Heaven’s life on earth. The Fall was a declaration of independence that let a pretender seize the colony; and from his Bahamian boyhood he shows what a bad governor takes from a people, their language, their history and their culture, as a picture of what sin stole from humanity and what the Kingdom restores.',
    inApp: 'Read chapter 1 of God’s Big Idea (the garden and the two ways kingdoms expand) and chapter 3 (the governors who took language, history and culture). Then read Genesis 2:8, Matthew 6:10 and Revelation 7:9 and weigh it by the Word: what did sin take from us, what does Jesus give back, and does the Kingdom erase the nations or gather them?',
