    honestNote: 'The chapter 1 and chapter 3 lines are from OCR text of a user-uploaded copy of the 2012 Destiny Image edition on archive.org; the p. ix and p. 12 lines were cross-checked against publisher-authorized Google Books pages of the 2010 edition, which confirm the same words. OCR glyph errors were corrected only in mechanical ways (for example "ol" to "of", "feet" to "fact"), and these short excerpts should be checked against a licensed print copy before wider publication. His word for the adversary in the quoted chapter 1 line is lowercase in his own text. The Kingdom-as-colony picture is his illustration; the Word’s own words are kingdom, citizenship and ambassadors, and the lesson says so. His hope for "one culture throughout the entire created realm" is weighed against Revelation 7:9 and 21:24, which show the nations still distinct before the throne; that is a correction of that one phrase, not of his larger point. The summaries of his argument are ours and marked as summary.',
